# Terraform
# Provider binaries and the local backend cache; regenerated by `terraform init`.
**/.terraform/
#
# .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored, in any root. It pins exact
# provider versions and checksums, which is what makes an apply reproducible and
# what stops a compromised provider release from being pulled silently.
#
# This matters most for terraform/sandbox: the builder copies that directory to a
# fresh temp dir and runs `terraform init` on every single provision. Without a
# committed lock, `~> 6.14` resolves to whatever is newest at that moment, so two
# sandboxes created a week apart can run different provider versions — a
# provider regression would reach production provisioning with no commit to
# bisect. The temp workspace is ephemeral; the source directory it is copied
# from is not, and neither is its lock file.
#
# Platforms: the lock records a per-platform `h1:` hash alongside the registry's
# `zh:` hashes. The `zh:` set covers every platform, so running `init` from a
# different OS/arch does not fail outright — it quietly appends an `h1:` and
# leaves you with an unexplained lock diff in your PR. The platforms below are
# already pre-recorded so that does not happen; re-run this if you add one:
#
#   terraform providers lock \
#     -platform=linux_amd64 -platform=darwin_arm64 -platform=darwin_amd64
#
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
# Rendered per-sandbox inputs. Contains the database password and app secret in
# plaintext, so it must never be committed.
*.tfvars.json
crash.log
